<title>POLAND: Farm Food pays PLN 3.1 mln for meat firm.</title>
<headline>Farm Food pays PLN 3.1 mln for meat firm.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish meat processing company paid the state treasury 3.1 million zlotys for a 55 percent stake in meat firm  Zaklady Miesne Miestar w Tarnowie SA, Farm Food said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>Farm Food said it also pledged to invest 12 million zlotys in the company in the next two years.</p>
<p>The remaining  20 percent of Miestar's shares are earmarked for employees, 20 percent for farm producers cooperating with the company and five percent for a planned state fund for restitution claims.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
